      <h2 id="olm-deleting-operator-from-a-cluster-using-cli_olm-deleting-operators-from-a-cluster" class="group scroll-mt-20">Deleting Operators from a cluster using the CLI<a href="#olm-deleting-operator-from-a-cluster-using-cli_olm-deleting-operators-from-a-cluster" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To remove an installed Operator from a namespace, cluster administrators can delete its subscription and cluster service version (CSV) by using the CLI.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have access to the OpenShift Container Platform cluster using an account with <code>cluster-admin</code> permissions.</li>
      <li>The OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>) is installed on your workstation.</li>
